config BR2_PACKAGE_FEX_EMU
	bool "fex-emu"
	depends on BR2_aarch64
	help
	  FEX is a fast usermode x86 and x86-64 emulator for arm64 Linux.
	  It JIT-translates x86(-64) instructions to arm64 and registers
	  itself with the kernel's binfmt_misc so x86(-64) ELF binaries
	  are transparently launched through it. This is the same
	  translation layer Valve bundles into Proton for Steam Frame /
	  SteamOS on arm64.

	  Running x86(-64) binaries also requires an x86 RootFS (fetched
	  at runtime via FEXRootFSFetcher) providing x86 shared libraries.

	  https://github.com/FEX-Emu/FEX
